{
  "case_id": "2011-11-262",
  "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nSEAN R. GALLAGHER, ESQ., Denver, Colorado; for Petitioners.\nSRI SRINIVASAN, ESQ., Principal Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Petitioners.\nDAVID A. LANE, ESQ., Denver, Colorado; for Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: There's just a little bit of noise in the courtroom, and I'm -- I have a little bit of difficulty hearing your very opening statement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GALLAGHER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The issue before the Court today is whether Secret Service agents who are prepared to take a bullet for the Vice President must also be prepared to take a retaliatory arrest lawsuit, even when they have probable cause to make an arrest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0000-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SRINIVASAN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to start off addressing the Secret Service in particular because that's the principal focus, although I take the point that there are questions about applying the rule in a broader context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: -- in front of this Court or anywhere for that matter? The people making the demonstration have -- have the same motivation and can make the same assertion of, oh, the only reason you arrested me was because you didn't like what I was -- what I was talking about. So, why should that situation be different?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have a sense of how many of these First Amendment retaliatory claims in those jurisdictions that permit them -- I know they're more limited -- how many of these cases arise?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners' counsel",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Right, and I can understand the basis for the nervousness. I guess the question for the Court is whether the benefits of having an administrable across-the-board rule outweigh the costs of trying to forge some sort exceptions to deal with extreme hypotheticals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And how many arrests are there a year?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You might apply the same immunity for selective enforcement based on race?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners' counsel",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. The -- they -- I think the Court's decision in Whren, for example, supposes that even though you have probable cause, you can have an equal protection claim if the proof could be made -- and this is very important."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what about for crowd control? You want to extend it to crowd control as well. What difference does the First Amendment make there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How many cases -- you might know this; you might have information on how many cases over 5 years or whatever period there actually have been against Federal protective officials of retaliatory First Amendment activity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent's counsel",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think what we have here is a solution being offered by the Government, and now we have to go find the problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And it wouldn't be a violation of the First Amendment if they only did that because they didn't like the ideas he was expressing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Is that -- is that a case that you could state?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LANE",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANE: Well, I mean, litigious plaintiffs are a consistent problem across the board under many contexts. And there's really -- you know, there's almost nothing that can be done. This Court has taken steps to cut back prison litigation that's frivolous, things of that nature."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: It's not a conclusion. I mean, if -- if he didn't have the bumper sticker and you asserted in the pleading he stopped me because he knows I hate the police, that's a conclusion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LANE",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANE: Well, I mean, these evidentiary questions have to be first of all supported in a pleading with heightened scrutiny under Iqbal. Conclusions are not simply enough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LANE",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANE: Theoretically, every single person who has ever been arrested for any crime could raise a first amendment retaliation lawsuit. Every convicted murderer doing time throughout this country could do that. They don't, however. There is -- there is not a rush to the courthouse of retaliatory arrest claims because the pleading requirements are heightened."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Would you acknowledge that the Secret Service faces a different situation from ordinary police officers in conducting their daily activities, in that Secret Service agents may legitimately take into account First Amendment activity by someone who is in the vicinity of the President or the Vice President in assessing the degree of danger the person presents?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LANE",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0010",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The status quo is Mount Healthy. It has worked for decades, and it should continue to work."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "66d4177b6de7ec597ce3c7f0a0e5306491df6d6773af2c88257e84eabb6970c3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-66d4177b6de7-0002-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 12:30 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
